Peripheral tests for the Arduino UNO Q (open firmware stack, agatti-next).

  ./run-all.sh          everything; screen/USB-host parts skip without a dock
  ./video.sh [N W H c]  venus encode/decode round trip (h264|h265)
  ./gpu.sh [N]          A702: kernel side, kmscube + glmark2 on the monitor
  ./display.sh [S]      DP connector, EDID, S seconds of colour bars
  ./weston.sh           Weston + demo clients on the monitor
  ./usb.sh [keys]       type-C role, devices behind the dock, keyboard
  ./bluetooth.sh [S]    WCN39xx firmware, BlueZ, S-second scan
  ./adsp.sh [N]         ADSP start/stop over OP-TEE PAS
  ./buses.sh            I2C, SPI (MCU), UARTs, QUP firmware
  ./tee.sh [full]       OP-TEE driver, PAS TA, xtest
  ./system.sh           CPUs, memory, eMMC, cpuidle/cpufreq
  ./audio.sh [S]        PM4125 headphone path: card, route, tone, power state
  ./audio-route.sh      route the card for playback/capture (used by audio.sh)
  ./wifi.sh [ssid psk]  modem (rmtfs/tqftpserv/QRTR), wlan0, scan; with credentials: associate + DHCP

Each script prints PASS/FAIL/SKIP lines and a summary; the exit status
is non-zero when something failed. Logs of the heavier steps land in
/tmp. Screen tests need the board on a type-C dock with a monitor.
Details: agatti_docs/notes/peripheral-testing.md on the build host.
